{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SUPERSEDED BY OPERATOR RULING — closing without implementing.\n\nThe operator ruled that a dedicated parent verb carrying --force is the right shape and is OUT OF SCOPE\nfor this session, and that the current store state is ACCEPTED so long as the affected tickets are all\nclosed. Filed as idea [rebar:5992-f317-e05e-42f7], which carries the full verified analysis of why no\nsupported reparent route exists.\n\nThe acceptance condition was checked, not assumed: of the 63 tickets whose parent was cleared, 61 are\nclosed. TWO were not — 437c-dd9d-9e65-46e7 (in_progress) and bf03-73bf-b66a-4c84 (open) — so those fell\noutside the acceptance and were REPAIRED. Both were repairable with a plain 'rebar edit --parent' and no\nforce at all, because their parents (9594-1f1c-bcd1-4774 and 4804-d9eb-e682-4d9c) are themselves still\nin_progress / open, so the closed-parent guard never engaged. Verified by re-reading the reduced tickets:\n437c parent_id='9594-1f1c-bcd1-4774', bf03 parent_id='4804-d9eb-e682-4d9c'.\n\nSo this ticket's premise — that the repair required a new capability — held only for the 61 closed\ntickets, whose state is now accepted. Nothing here is implemented and nothing is pending on it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785773530681140001,"uuid":"4a5b266e-b429-4e07-91dc-3217f26f3ebe"}